  "max_pan_per_s": 0.85,
  "max_tilt_per_s": 0.95,
  "note": "Max ANGULAR VELOCITY as a fraction of range per second. That is the number that governs a recipe -- NOT full-range travel time, which an earlier version of this file confused it with. A good head reaches 400-600 deg/s, so on a 540 deg pan that is 0.74-1.11 range/s. This club rig is mid-range hardware, so 0.85 pan / 0.95 tilt; a fast fixture takes 1.05/1.15 and a cheap one half of that. The recipe DERIVES its amplitude from this budget rather than being checked against it, so it cannot ask a motor for more than the motor has -- which is why lowering this number makes the show gentler instead of making the test fail."
 },
